# Script Documentation

Every script in `scripts/` must have a matching man-page-style doc at `docs/scripts/<script_name>.md`.

- When you **create** a script `scripts/foo.py`, also create `docs/scripts/foo.md`.
- When you **update** a script, update `docs/scripts/<script_name>.md` to match.

## Doc file structure

```markdown
# foo

Short one-line description.

## Synopsis

    python scripts/foo.py [OPTIONS]

## Description

What the script does, in a few sentences.

## Options

| Flag | Default | Description |
|------|---------|-------------|
| `--bar` | `baz` | What --bar does |

## Examples

    python scripts/foo.py --bar value

## Output

What files or stdout the script produces.
```
